===Etymology 2===
[[File:Agrostemma githago 1.jpg|thumb]]
{{wikipedia|Lolium temulentum}}
{{wikipedia|Agrostemma githago}}
{{wikispecies|Lolium temulentum}}
{{wikispecies|Agrostemma githago}}
From {{inh|en|enm|cockil}}, {{m|enm|cokil}}, {{m|enm|cokylle}}, from {{inh|en|ang|coccel|t=darnel}}, of unknown origin, perhaps from a diminutive of {{der|en|la|coccus||berry}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# Any of several field [[weed]]s, such as the {{vern|common corncockle}} ({{taxfmt|Agrostemma githago|species}}) and {{vern|darnel ryegrass}} ({{taxfmt|Lolium temulentum|species}}).
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1855|author=w:Robert Browning|title=s:Childe Roland to the Dark Tower Came|section=X
|passage=But '''cockle''', spurge, according to their law / Might propagate their kind, with none to awe, / You'd think; a burr had been a treasure trove.}}

